{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02212",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.03,
      "end_seconds": 4.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.26,
      "end_seconds": 11.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.73,
      "end_seconds": 20.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.85,
      "end_seconds": 26.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "So, yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.35,
      "end_seconds": 34.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Um, so... a hot red swollen big toe. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.34,
      "end_seconds": 39.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.35,
      "end_seconds": 44.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I mean, it's been two days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.85,
      "end_seconds": 51.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.1,
      "end_seconds": 73.74,
      "duration_seconds": 20.64,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say. I notice it more with touch. Well, I've had pain that woke me too, for two months. As for pain that woke me, it's all the time. I had not being able to wear a shoe before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.23,
      "end_seconds": 77.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Did you notice any rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.3,
      "end_seconds": 82.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "I mean, not that I've noticed, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 86.7,
      "end_seconds": 92.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice rash. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.34,
      "end_seconds": 101.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Oh, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.22,
      "end_seconds": 110.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. A few quick ones: fever or injury?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.18,
      "end_seconds": 113.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.99,
      "end_seconds": 118.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "So, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.44,
      "end_seconds": 122.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.35,
      "end_seconds": 126.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.24,
      "end_seconds": 133.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.43,
      "end_seconds": 137.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 138.97,
      "end_seconds": 144.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "She takes metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.81,
      "end_seconds": 148.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "How long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 152.72,
      "end_seconds": 163.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "About three months now. Ah, she is on allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day for the gout, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.72,
      "end_seconds": 167.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "How long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 168.53,
      "end_seconds": 173.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "For two years. Actually, she takes iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.44,
      "end_seconds": 178.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.73,
      "end_seconds": 180.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.41,
      "end_seconds": 185.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Okay, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.97,
      "end_seconds": 200.2,
      "duration_seconds": 13.23,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. My partner and our baby. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.6,
      "end_seconds": 214.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.05,
      "end_seconds": 224.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years. Yes, gout. I have low haemoglobin, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.44,
      "end_seconds": 232.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high blood pressure and gout in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.39,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Right, I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.35,
      "end_seconds": 258.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.46,
      "end_seconds": 291.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.54,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 119 over 78, BMI works out to 17.9, weight 58 kilos, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pulse 86, height 180 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.66,
      "end_seconds": 295.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.75,
      "end_seconds": 303.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.25,
      "end_seconds": 309.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.01,
      "end_seconds": 312.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.88,
      "end_seconds": 330.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "The big toe joint is red, hot, swollen and exquisitely tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.85,
      "end_seconds": 337.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.71,
      "end_seconds": 359.84,
      "duration_seconds": 11.13,
      "text": "Let me just check I've got this right. You've had a hot red swollen big toe for two days, mild, and no injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.23,
      "end_seconds": 363.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.99,
      "end_seconds": 373.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Kidney function tests is what I'd like next, for gout treatment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.22,
      "end_seconds": 376.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "How long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.73,
      "end_seconds": 396.3,
      "duration_seconds": 15.57,
      "text": "Let's book a uric acid blood test to look into gout. I'd like you to take naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, five days. You take it by mouth. It's for gout flare."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.15,
      "end_seconds": 402.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "That's simple enough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.31,
      "end_seconds": 423.16,
      "duration_seconds": 18.85,
      "text": "Rest the foot, ice it, and drink plenty of water; limit beer and red meat. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.79,
      "end_seconds": 427.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}